  "verifiedAt": "2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z",
  "intro": "The area between two curves $y=f(x)$ (top) and $y=g(x)$ (bottom) from $x=a$ to $x=b$ is $\\int_a^b [f(x)-g(x)]\\,dx$, provided $f\\ge g$ on the interval. First find the intersection points to set the limits, then integrate top minus bottom. If the curves cross, split the integral where they switch. When regions are easier horizontally, integrate right minus left in $y$ instead.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Find the area between $y=x$ and $y=x^2$ from their intersections.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Set $x=x^2$: $x^2-x=0\\Rightarrow x(x-1)=0$, so intersections at $x=0$ and $x=1$.",
          "On $(0,1)$, $y=x$ is above $y=x^2$, so integrate $x-x^2$.",
          "$\\int_0^1 (x-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_0^1=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}$.",
          "Combine: $\\frac{1}{6}$."
        ],
        "answer": "Area $=\\dfrac{1}{6}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Find the area between $y=4-x^2$ and the x-axis.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "The parabola meets the axis where $4-x^2=0\\Rightarrow x=\\pm 2$.",
          "The region is above the axis on $[-2,2]$, so integrate $4-x^2$.",
          "$\\int_{-2}^{2}(4-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[4x-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{-2}^{2}=\\left(8-\\frac{8}{3}\\right)-\\left(-8+\\frac{8}{3}\\right)=\\frac{32}{3}$."
        ],
        "answer": "Area $=\\dfrac{32}{3}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Find the area between $y=x^2$ and $y=2x$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Set $x^2=2x$: $x^2-2x=0\\Rightarrow x=0,2$.",
          "On $(0,2)$, the line $2x$ is above the parabola, so integrate $2x-x^2$.",
          "$\\int_0^2 (2x-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[x^2-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_0^2=4-\\frac{8}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}$."
        ],
        "answer": "Area $=\\dfrac{4}{3}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "Area between $y=x^2$ and $y=x$ ... already shown; find area between $y=6-x^2$ and $y=x$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Intersections: $6-x^2=x\\Rightarrow x^2+x-6=0\\Rightarrow x=-3,2$.",
          "Top is $6-x^2$; $\\int_{-3}^{2}(6-x^2-x)\\,dx=\\frac{125}{6}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{125}{6}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 5,
      "prompt": "Area between $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and $y=x$ from $0$ to $1$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "On $(0,1)$, $\\sqrt{x}\\ge x$; $\\int_0^1(\\sqrt{x}-x)\\,dx=\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{6}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{6}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 6,
      "prompt": "Area enclosed between $y=x^3$ and $y=x$ on $[0,1]$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "On $(0,1)$, $x\\ge x^3$; $\\int_0^1(x-x^3)\\,dx=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{4}$"
      }
    }
  ]
